  evidence:
  - evidence_type: CURATOR_JUDGMENT
    source: https://togomedium.org/medium/M491
    notes: 'TOGO M491 provides the explicit prepared basal grouping and preparation
      comment. Its original JCM490 endpoint capture says Nothing found; no successful
      original formulation inspection is claimed. TOGO groups phosphate salts with
      this base, unlike M481; the provider-defined version is preserved without declaring
      equality to JCM480. Source transcription basis (literal input amounts, not calculated
      stock concentrations): distilled water: 900 ml; MgSO4・7H2O: 0.5 g; Yeast extract:
      0.5 g; NaCl: 2.25 g; CaCl2・2H2O: 0.25 g; KH2PO4: 0.227 g; NH4Cl: 0.5 g; K2HPO4:
      0.348 g; Resazurin: 1 mg; Casitone (BD-Difco): 0.5 g; Trace vitamins (see Medium
      [M190]): 10 ml; Trace element solution (see Medium No. [480]): 1 ml; Se/W solution
      (see Medium [M312]): 1 ml. No batch-to-final-volume conversion is made. Handling
      atmosphere is not listed as a material part; pH reagents are source inputs,
      without an assertion of unchanged molecular species after pH adjustment. Nested
      formulations remain source-qualified named parts where exact composition/owner
      identity is not established. No verified exact eligible ontology term or existing
      whole-preparation owner was established by the bounded source/owner review.
      This self-registry mapping represents the preparation, not its individual constituents.'
